GONIX LAB
=========

A second, separate Nginx for trying GoNix safely. Nothing here touches the
system's Nginx ({{ .SystemConfig }}) or its service.

  Directory     {{ .Dir }}
  Nginx         systemd unit {{ .Unit }} ({{ if .Active }}running{{ else }}stopped{{ end }}), config {{ .Dir }}/nginx.conf
  Ports         HTTP {{ .HTTPPort }}, HTTPS {{ .HTTPSPort }} (certificates are self-signed)
  Backends      {{ .BackendA }} answers "backend A", {{ .BackendB }} answers "backend B"
  GoNix         instance "{{ .Instance }}" ({{ .InstanceFile }})

WORKING IN THE LAB
------------------
TUI:  Lab > Enter Lab. The title bar says "{{ .Instance }}" and every screen works
      on the lab. "Exit Lab" in its main menu returns here.
CLI:  every command takes --instance {{ .Instance }}, for example:

  sudo gonix --instance {{ .Instance }} host list
  sudo gonix --instance {{ .Instance }} adopt --all --dry-run
  sudo gonix --instance {{ .Instance }} history show <commit>   # the exact diff of a change

Requests to the test domains, without editing /etc/hosts:

  t() { local h=${1#*://}; h=${h%%/*}; h=${h%%:*}
        curl -sk -i --resolve "$h:{{ .HTTPPort }}:127.0.0.1" --resolve "$h:{{ .HTTPSPort }}:127.0.0.1" "$@"; }
  t http://<domain>:{{ .HTTPPort }}/
  t https://<domain>:{{ .HTTPSPort }}/

